From: bentrd <benj.tordjman@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 11:52:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wiki: document the gambit UI explanation flags and the rest
 of ModGambitApi

The Show* builder calls were listed with no explanation of what each one
does, so modders had to open GambitDefinition.cs to see what they could
use. API Reference now tables all fourteen flags with the exact vanilla
explainer box each one adds (title + wording, from the game's text data),
the matching <color>/<sprite> description markup, the enable-what-your-
description-uses rule, and the flagless ADJACENT PIECE exception.
Your First Gambit gets a compact version of the same, explaining the
.ShowLanding() its example already used.

Also fills other reference gaps:
- ModGambitApi documented only LoadSprite; adds CreateGambit, Register/
  RegisterAll for hand-built definitions, Unlock (and how it differs from
  AutoUnlock's retry queue), and LoadSprite's pivot parameter
- name/description localization behaviour: injected under <id>_name /
  <id>_description, re-injected on language change, one string for all
  eleven languages
