+### UI explanation flags — the `Show*` calls
+
+The `.ShowLanding()` in the example is why Lucky Penny's card gets vanilla's
+little LANDING explainer box ("Placing a piece from stock to board during a
+game.") next to its description wherever the card is inspected — shop,
+collection, and mid-run. Each keyword mechanic in the game has a box like
+that, and the builder has fourteen flags for them, all off by default:
+
+| Flag | Explainer it adds |
+| ---- | ----------------- |
+| `.ShowGolden()` / `.ShowGoldenTile()` | GOLDEN PIECE / GOLDEN TILE |
+| `.ShowBless()` / `.ShowBlessedTile()` | BLESSED PIECE / BLESS TILE |
+| `.ShowProtect()` / `.ShowProtectedTile()` | PROTECTED PIECE / PROTECT TILE |
+| `.ShowTrap()` / `.ShowTrapTile()` | TRAPPED PIECE / TRAP TILE |
+| `.ShowPhantom()` / `.ShowPhantomTile()` | PHANTOM PIECE / PHANTOM TILE |
+| `.ShowLanding()` | LANDING |
+| `.ShowWait()` | WAIT |
+| `.ShowPromotion()` | PROMOTION |
+| `.ShowConsideredAs()` | COUNTED AS |
+
+The rule: **turn on the flag for every keyword your description uses**, and
+no others. The piece flags explain a piece state; the `*Tile` flags explain
+the tile that applies that state. The boxes are display-only and come
+pre-translated into the game's eleven languages — one more reason to build on
+vanilla vocabulary instead of inventing your own terms.
+
+Vanilla's exact wording for every box, plus which `<color>`/`<sprite>` markup
+pairs with which flag, is tabled in the
+[API Reference](API-Reference#ui-explanation-flags).
+
 ### `WithBaseGambit<T>()` vs `OnTrigger()`
 
 The builder clones a vanilla gambit prefab as a template.
